  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">**Negative (the NFR-02 gate):** given a user denied Read on a matter that has documents indexed in `documentVector3072`, when that user calls `GET /api/ai/visualization/related/{documentId}` with a source document whose neighbors include that matter's documents, then **none** of that matter's documents appear in the response. This is a passing automated test, not a checklist item.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">**Negative:** the same assertion holds for `POST /api/ai/visualization/related-from-content`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the per-row-authorization signal is absent from `HttpContext.Items`, when either visualization route is invoked, then it returns 500 and serves zero rows — the fail-closed forcing function copied from `RecordSearchEndpoints.cs:117-129`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a mixed result set of permitted and denied rows, when the route returns, then the returned count equals the number of **permitted** rows — it does not reveal the pre-trim total.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given no user token on the request, when the access check runs, then it resolves `AccessRights.None` and no app-only fallback occurs.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`POST /api/ai/visualization/related-from-content` has an authorization filter attached at the route or group level (ADR-008) — verified by the arch guard, not by inspection alone.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`Api/Ai/VisualizationEndpoints.cs` appears in `GovernedFiles` in `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RouteAuthorizationGuardTests.cs`, and `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests` passes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The negative test was verified to FAIL when the per-row check is temporarily disabled, and that verification is recorded in `notes/032-authorization-hardening.md`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Per-row verdicts are memoized per record within a request, and the check is bounded by a maximum-checks constant mirroring `MaxRecordAuthorizationChecks:207`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">BFF publish size was measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with PowerShell `Compress-Archive`; both absolute sizes, delta and tool are recorded; delta &lt;+5 MB and absolute &lt;60 MB.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR description contains a Placement Justification section per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All unit, contract and arch tests pass; `dotnet build` is green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md NFR-02 and FR-16; plan.md §3 finding F-b and risk R-3 ("If hardening proves large, Find is cut from r1 rather than shipped unsafe"). This task gates 033 structurally — do not begin the Find view on an unhardened surface. Record the measured per-row latency at the default limit in `notes/` so 033 can size its result page against real numbers.
  </notes>

